# Presentation-golden corpus manifest for Spyro 3 (fields as in
# games/spyro-1/corpus/presentation-corpus.manifest: name|start|interval|freeze|pins).
# The level loads by VBL ~1414 under --skip-to-level and gameplay is live by
# ~1773; 2073 leaves the fade settled.
# The pin holds VBL 2073 on the sub-tick leg as well as the canonical one: the
# grid's intermediate samples land at +interval/2, so the pose the player walk
# was measured against had no __inter__ tile of its own.
# 3133 pins the camera inside the portal (VBLs 3117-3162), where the
# destination's preview picture fills the screen.
# 3273 pins the level transition past the grid's last sample: the movie's
# inputs end at 3162 and the run continues, so the sub-tick leg there is
# the transition gamestate, where the re-extract draws the cyclorama and the
# player and every other producer returns empty. The grid's own 3223
# intermediate sample covers the transition's start; 3273 covers it 50 VBLs
# further in, where the canonical frame no longer moves between ticks.
# 2239: Bianca's trail effect blends toward dark where the PSX blends toward
# light; blessed pre-fix.
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry|2073|100||2073,2239,3133,3273
# @tcache / @tcsqueeze: the retained terrain cache forced on (llvmpipe refuses it
# otherwise) across a level edge; @tcsqueeze also sizes every arena primary at
# 32768 elements (OPENPETE_TC_INITIAL_CAP) so the arenas grow mid-level. Coverage
# rows of the arena-growth path: the image must match the unsqueezed run.
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry@tcache|2073|100||2073,3273|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off
# @tcbudget0: the first-touch bake budget at 0 (one sector baked per tick), pinned
# through bake-in, where deferred sectors are drawn by the CPU walk beside
# retained ones; a change at that seam moves these tiles. The other
# cache-forced rows turn the budget off, since a wall-time budget makes the
# walked set differ between runs.
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry@tcbudget0|577|200||577,1577|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=0
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry@tcsqueeze|2073|100||2073,3273|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_INITIAL_CAP=32768 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off

# sunrise-spring-surface-swim arms the player draw's water-plane split.
# g_Spyro+0x28 is zero on every frame of the other three bk2s and of the whole
# 20k attract demo (six levels); it is non-zero from VBL 2462 to this movie's
# end, with animationState 0x2B (SWIM_MOVE_SURFACE) and movementState 0x0A
# (SWIM_SURFACE), so the split's classification, its depth cue and its cut have
# no other row in the corpus.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim|2473|150||2473,2573,2773
# sunrise-spring-surface-swim@heldfade: a present of the held-fade loop after
# the loading screen (isbg=0, one subtractive quad per VBL over the held picture).
sunrise-spring-surface-swim@heldfade|1554|100|freeze|1556
# sunrise-spring-surface-swim@entry: the level-entry loading screen, where the
# game keeps its picture in VRAM (isbg=0) and draws only the progress strip.
# No freeze field: the headless capture keeps the retained backdrop on its own.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim@entry|1500|100||1500
# sunrise-spring-surface-swim@simplebase: the camera follows the swim past the
# simple-moby gems (class 0x0C8) at the right of the frame. A simple moby's cull
# record holds its camera-relative position truncated to 4 world units
# (mobydraw.s:81,87,94), and the residue the truncation drops changes every
# tick the camera moves. Over VBLs 2473-2591 the gem at 0x8018DD0C has the
# largest step between the end of one tick's sub-tick run and the start of the
# next, 0.42 px, at this VBL; the sub-tick tile shows the gem half a tick in.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim@simplebase|2541|100||2541

# icy-peak-reflective-mirror arms the player draw's mirrored copy.
# g_Spyro+0x2C is the avatar's height above a material-class-4 surface; of the
# 37 levels only Icy Peak, Midday Gardens, Frozen Altars and Bugbot Factory
# carry a class-4 material at all, and the word is zero on every frame of the
# other four bk2s and of the whole 20k attract demo. Icy Peak spawns beside
# such a surface: idle to VBL 1873, then Up + Circle (charge) with a 60-frame
# Right every 400 to hold the rink, and the word is non-zero from VBL 2431 to
# this movie's end, so the reflection's matrix negation, its inverted
# back-face test and its ordering bias have no other row in the corpus. The
# pins are the frames where the copy is least occluded by the surface above
# it: 5011 to 7167 pixels of the frame move when the reflection is suppressed,
# against 588 to 1421 on the grid samples after 2598.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror|2473|150||2473,2494,2523,2534,2573,2574
# icy-peak-reflective-mirror@1856: the same movie at the tick that shows
# Spyro's reflection on the ice (VBL 2429), before the row above starts; the
# player colour-block swap is measured here.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror@1856|2429|600||2429
# icy-peak-reflective-mirror@1864: the same movie where the player shadow fan,
# cast onto the reflective floor's plane, lands on the ice ramp that stands
# above that plane; the decal's raised-occluder test is measured here.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror@1864|2437|600||2437,2443
# icy-peak-reflective-mirror@wall: Spyro's mirrored copy in front of the
# reflected ice wall; native drew only the tail tip, the copy pushed
# behind the reflected wall in depth. Blessed pre-fix.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror@wall|2703|600||2703
# an-evil-plot-unfolds-egg-edge: the opening cutscene under 16:9; animated-model
# mobys inside the cull's distance box that fail its 4:3 lateral arm get no
# widened-view re-admission, so two eggs are absent from the right band at 1779
# and 1783. The left egg's disappearance between 1781 and 1782 is the game
# moving it (its 4:3 staging, kept).
an-evil-plot-unfolds-egg-edge|1773|10||1773,1779,1783,1793|--skip-to-cutscene an_evil_plot_unfolds
# a-powerful-villain-emerges-throne: the throne record switches clip at VBL 5641
# after a static span; the interp store's dedupe stretches its pair across the
# span, the COUNTSW hold re-derives the previous pose from a header the game
# has rewritten, and the throne vanishes on intermediate presents 5643-5731.
a-powerful-villain-emerges-throne|5653|10||5667|--skip-to-cutscene a_powerful_villain_emerges
# no-hard-feelings-sheila-portal: the Sheila's Alp portal (record level 16)
# opens in this cutscene; its picture is baked from Sunny Villa's sky, not its
# destination's, so the destination-sky extension leaves the 16:9 left band
# showing the flat backdrop. VBL 3304 is openpete_frame 2731 under this boot.
no-hard-feelings-sheila-portal|3304|10||3304|--skip-to-cutscene no_hard_feelings
# no-hard-feelings-sheila-portal@heldcut: the cutscene's second camera cut
# lands on the tick at VBL 2513 (openpete_frame 1941), from a shot with the
# portal in view to one of Spyro without it. The intermediate present at 2513
# holds tick 2511's camera across the cut and lost the portal's previews,
# which it took from tick 2513's capture. 2511 is the last canonical tick
# before the cut. Blessed pre-fix.
no-hard-feelings-sheila-portal@heldcut|2513|10||2511,2513|--skip-to-cutscene no_hard_feelings
# the-end-shell-gateway: the end credits, scene 1 (Seashell Shore terrain);
# the right inner edge of the pink shell gateway flickers at VBL 5912
# (openpete_frame 5339 after the 573-VBL fast boot). Blessed pre-fix.
the-end-shell-gateway|5905|2||5905,5907,5909,5911,5912,5913,5915,5917|--skip-to-cutscene the_end
# the-end-portal-rim: scene 1, the bottom-left outer rim of the octagonal
# portal seen from above flickers at VBL 7046 (openpete_frame 6473).
the-end-portal-rim|7039|2||7041,7043,7045,7046,7047,7049,7051|--skip-to-cutscene the_end
# the-end-icy-peak-pop: scene 2 (Icy Peak terrain), a cliff-band triangle at
# the right edge of the 16:9 frame (x 756-789, y 175-191 of 853x432) changes
# between the ticks around VBL 7910 (openpete_frame 7337) at --lod extended.
the-end-icy-peak-pop|7901|2||7905,7907,7909,7910,7911,7913|--skip-to-cutscene the_end
# the-end-haunted-tomb-archway: scene 9 (Haunted Tomb terrain), a side face
# of the archway shows through the wall left of its top at VBL 20570
# (openpete_frame 19997); the -og reference shows it too.
the-end-haunted-tomb-archway|20565|2||20567,20569,20570,20571|--skip-to-cutscene the_end

# sunrise-spring-camera-swing holds R2 from VBL 2073 so the camera orbits the
# player while two animated mobys and the simple-model gems, baskets and
# chest stay in view. The pins hold sub-tick presents mid-swing, where an
# animated record replayed in the tick camera's view space is displaced from
# the interpolated camera by half a tick of rotation.
# 2333 and 2573 pin the swing's distant-band poses, where the far world is HP
# geometry under --lod extended and the sub-tick re-extract has the most to
# lose. They cover the pose, not the sector-occlusion class itself: the
# occluder depth grid is a GPU readback and headless holds none, so a headless
# tile cannot see a cull verdict change. That class is measured windowed, per
# walk.
# 2329 (lod extended canonical): the terrain feed of the world draw used the
# previous tick's portal openings while this tick's portal pass captured a
# different set; a sliver shows through the arch edge. Blessed pre-fix.
# 2400, 2440, 2480, 2540: the camera moves 38 units per tick on average here
# (VBLs 2380-2569) past mobys resting on terrain, so the sub-tick tiles hold
# moby-against-terrain contact under a moving camera.
sunrise-spring-camera-swing|2073|100||2091,2092,2093,2113,2133,2329,2333,2400,2440,2480,2540,2573
# sunrise-spring-camera-swing@glintdepth: the same movie under a fixed freecam
# pose engaged at VBL 2100, a gem's near star close to the camera. The star
# took its pool record's view-Z, which lies inside the gem, so the gem's own
# front faces hid part of it (2111) and the ground beneath cut its lower
# spikes (2271). The row above pins 2113, where a crest nearer than the gem
# still hides the star. Blessed pre-fix.
sunrise-spring-camera-swing@glintdepth|2271|600||2111,2271|OPENPETE_FREECAM_AT_VBL=2100 OPENPETE_FREECAM_POSE=33676,23337,16122,0,224

# 2073 pins the opening dialogue, complete and static from 2067: a large
# semi-transparent text box whose corners are semi-transparent textured quads.
# sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible: Sheila, the playable moby, turns invisible
# in the water at VBL 5129; that pin holds the present on both legs. The 5093 pin
# holds a sub-tick present while she moves through the world under a moving
# camera: her own motion must interpolate as her camera-relative motion does.
# 5067, 5071, 5081, 5085 and 5101 hold sub-tick presents while Sheila and the
# NPCs beside her blend into their next animations.
sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible|4973|100||2073,5067,5071,5081,5085,5093,5101,5129

